Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the improper handling of the scatter-gather (sg) list during multi-block read and write operations. Specifically, the code did not advance the sg_miter to the first entry before starting to read or write blocks, nor did it check for the availability of the next entry immediately after processing a block. This oversight could lead to a situation where the last block is processed without confirming if there are more entries, resulting in a timeout when no further data is available and no subsequent interrupt occurs.

